  <section id="mechanism" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="mechanism-title">
    <div class="slide-inner taskvector-slide taskvector-method-slide">
      <h2 id="mechanism-title">{t('参数确实在变，但它们到底朝哪里变？', 'The parameters are changing, but which way are they moving?')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('TaskVector 可以理解成一支“参数方向箭头”：把一次学习前后的参数相减，就能看参数移动了多少、连续更新是否同向，以及拿掉这段参数变化后行为会不会跟着变。它只负责诊断参数变化，最终 WebShop 成绩仍由冻结终评回答。', 'Think of a TaskVector as a parameter-direction arrow: subtract parameters before and after learning to measure how far they moved, whether successive updates align, and whether behavior changes when that accumulated change is removed. It is a diagnostic; the frozen final still determines WebShop performance.')}</p>
      <div class="taskvector-equation" aria-label={t('TaskVector 定义', 'TaskVector definition')}>
        <span>TaskVector</span>
        <strong>v = θ<sub>after</sub> − θ<sub>before</sub></strong>
        <p>{t('θ 是模型参数；v 是这一次学习真正走过的参数方向。', 'θ denotes model parameters; v is the parameter direction taken by this learning step.')}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="taskvector-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><strong>{t('看移动多少', 'measure distance')}</strong><p>{t('‖v‖ 看参数移动的大小。', '‖v‖ measures how far the parameters moved.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><strong>{t('看方向是否一致', 'compare direction')}</strong><p>{t('cosine 看相邻更新是顺着前一次继续走，还是开始往不同方向拉。', 'Cosine shows whether adjacent updates continue in a similar direction or begin pulling apart.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><strong>{t('看行为会不会变', 'test behavior')}</strong><p>{t('拿掉累计 SD-LoRA 参数变化后，固定 24 个输入的第一选择全部翻转：24 / 24。说明这段参数变化已经进入决策过程。', 'After removing the accumulated SD-LoRA change, the top choice flipped on all 24 fixed inputs: 24 / 24. The parameter change is already affecting decisions.')}</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="taskvector-paper"><strong>{t('参考与证据', 'Reference and evidence')}</strong><a href={taskArithmeticHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Task Arithmetic ↗</a><span>{t('论文提供“把微调前后参数差看成方向”的背景；OpenEVO 的 24 / 24 行为干预来自我们自己的参数机制实验。', 'The paper motivates treating before/after parameter differences as directions; the 24 / 24 behavior intervention comes from our own OpenEVO mechanism experiment.')}</span></p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={measurementPackHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={measurementPackHref} /> PR #317 · {t('参数行为干预证据', 'parameter behavior intervention')}</a> · <a href={technicalHref}>{t('完整 TaskVector 推导', 'full TaskVector derivation')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">14 / 22</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="m1a-identifiability" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="m1a-title">
    <div class="slide-inner m1a-slide">
      <h2 id="m1a-title">{t('第一次量“末段参数方向”时，75% 和 100% 其实是同一个模型状态', 'Our first late-direction measurement used the same model state for 75% and 100%')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('这是一次值得保留的科研自我修正。原 M1-A 按训练进度取 25% / 50% / 75% / 100% 四个锚点，但真正解析到保存下来的已接受参数状态时，它们是 R27 / R49 / R49 / R49。R14、R27、R49 这类编号表示训练过程中保存下来的不同参数状态。', 'This is an important scientific self-correction. The original M1-A chose 25% / 50% / 75% / 100% progress anchors, but the saved accepted parameter states resolved to R27 / R49 / R49 / R49. Labels such as R14, R27, and R49 denote distinct saved parameter states from training.')}</p>
      <div class="m1a-grid">
        <article class="m1a-old"><span>{t('原设计', 'original design')}</span><strong>75% = 100% = R49</strong><p>{t('最后两个“测量点”其实是同一份参数，所以 θ₁₀₀% − θ₇₅% = 0。这个 0 说明实验没有能力分辨最后一段方向。', 'The last two measurement points are the same parameters, so θ₁₀₀% − θ₇₅% = 0. That zero means the design cannot distinguish the final direction segment.')}</p></article>
        <article class="m1a-fix"><span>{t('修订取点', 'corrected anchors')}</span><strong>R14 → R27 → R49</strong><p>{t('successor 改用相邻且互不相同的已接受参数状态，先保证每个测量点真的代表不同模型。', 'The successor uses adjacent, distinct accepted parameter states so each measurement point represents a genuinely different model.')}</p></article>
        <article class="m1a-result"><span>{t('恢复可辨识性', 'identifiability restored')}</span><strong>‖θ<sub>R49</sub> − θ<sub>R27</sub>‖ = 0.6082257746</strong><p>{t('末段向量严格非零，因此这个方向现在可以被测量。它只修复“能不能量”的问题；任务能力有没有提高仍要靠 WebShop 行为与冻结评测。', 'The late vector is strictly non-zero, so the direction is now measurable. This repairs the measurement question only; WebShop behavior and frozen evaluation still determine capability.')}</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="m1a-boundary"><strong>{t('我们改掉的判断', 'What changed in our judgment')}</strong>{t('看到零向量时，先检查两个端点是否真的是不同状态。这里原实验得到的是 measurement not identifiable；“参数最后没有变化”这个因果结论没有证据支持。', 'When a vector is zero, first verify that its endpoints are genuinely different states. The original result here was measurement not identifiable; it did not support a causal conclusion that the parameters stopped changing.')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={m1aPr350Href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={m1aPr350Href} /> PR #350 · {t('原 M1-A 取点失去可辨识性', 'original M1-A non-identifiability')}</a> · <a href={m1aPr358Href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={m1aPr358Href} /> PR #358 · {t('相邻互异状态修订', 'distinct-state successor')}</a> · <a href={technicalHref}>{t('完整几何证据', 'full geometry')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">15 / 22</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="gdr" class="briefing-slide tone-rose" aria-labelledby="gdr-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="gdr-title">{t('训练好的参数更新，为什么很多没有进入下一轮模型？', 'Why did many trained parameter updates never enter the next model state?')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('GDR 这个名字来自 Gated Delta Rule。Gated Delta Networks 论文提供的是 fast-memory 更新背景；我们真正运行的 GDR-v1 是自己的 operational admission rule：先训练完整候选，再用固定 16-task probe 看短期任务表现，决定候选是否进入下一轮。论文机制和本地执行定义需要分开读。', 'GDR is named after Gated Delta Rule. The Gated Delta Networks paper provides fast-memory-update background; our executed GDR-v1 is an operational admission rule of our own: train the full candidate, then use a fixed 16-task probe on short-horizon task behavior to decide whether it enters the next state. The paper mechanism and local execution definition must be read separately.')}</p>
      <div class="gdr-paper-map" aria-label={t('Gated Delta Rule 论文里的变量', 'Variables in the Gated Delta Rule paper')}>
        <div><span>S</span><strong>{t('当前 fast-memory state', 'current fast-memory state')}</strong></div>
        <div><span>k</span><strong>{t('要改写的关联位置', 'association address')}</strong></div>
        <div><span>v</span><strong>{t('准备写入的新 value', 'new value to write')}</strong></div>
        <p>{t('公式直觉是沿 k 修正旧关联，再把 v 写入状态；gating 控制这次写入有多强。', 'The equation corrects the old association along k, writes v into the state, and uses gating to control write strength.')}</p>
        <a href={gatedDeltaPaperHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Yang et al. · Gated Delta Networks ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="before-after gdr-flow">
        <div class="before"><span>{t('论文给我们的启发', 'paper inspiration')}</span><strong>{t('修正旧关联，再写入新信息', 'correct the old association, then write the new information')}</strong><p>{t('这个思想解释了为什么我们一开始会把 GDR 看成一种“擦掉旧方向、写入新方向”的参数更新思路。', 'This idea explains why we initially treated GDR as a parameter-update idea that removes an old direction and writes a new one.')}</p></div>
        <div class="after"><span>{t('我们真正跑的 GDR-v1', 'our executed GDR-v1')}</span><strong>{t('当前 OpenEVO 状态 + 完整候选状态 → 16-task probe → 是否采用', 'current OpenEVO state plus full candidate state → 16-task probe → admission decision')}</strong><p>{t('这里的 state 是整套 OpenEVO 运行状态和候选运行状态；v / k 没有直接映射成某个 SD-LoRA 张量。gate 用短期任务表现判断候选是否进入下一轮。', 'Here, state means the full OpenEVO running state and the candidate running state; v / k are not directly mapped to a specific SD-LoRA tensor. The gate uses short-horizon task behavior to decide whether the candidate enters the next round.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="gdr-why-gate"><strong>{t('为什么采用 gate 版本？', 'Why use a gate version?')}</strong>{t('当时还不能可靠判断哪段参数该擦、擦多少、哪段方向更正确，所以先使用可测任务表现作保守替代：候选先训练，再由 probe 决定是否进入下一轮。这个选择产生新的科学问题：短期不退步的准入，会不会提前截断长期有价值的更新？', 'At that point we could not reliably identify which parameter segment should be removed, how much to remove, or which new direction was correct. We therefore used measurable task behavior as a conservative substitute: train the candidate, then let the probe decide whether it enters the next round. This creates a new scientific question: can a short-horizon non-regression gate cut off updates that would become valuable later?')}</p>
      <p class="bottom-claim">{t('因此我们把两个计数分开看：OpenEVO 训练出了多少个 SD-LoRA 候选，以及 GDR 最终让多少个候选真正更新到后续模型。下一页就是 1.7B 正式线的实际结果。', 'We therefore track two counts separately: how many SD-LoRA candidates OpenEVO trained, and how many GDR allowed to update later model states. The next slide shows the formal 1.7B result.')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('GDR 的完整判定逻辑与实验定义', 'Full GDR decision logic and experiment definition')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">16 / 22</p>
    </div>
  </section>
